) is running."]}, "overview": "Florida's 26th District pairs ten-term Republican incumbent Mario Díaz-Balart with Democratic challenger Nicole Locklin and a minor independent candidate in a seat drawn with a seven-point Republican lean. Díaz-Balart has raised about $2.1 million and holds $2.5 million on hand, dwarfing Locklin's $348,000 raised, and he enters the fall unscathed after securing renomination under the new map. Every major rating outlet, including Cook, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball, and Split Ticket, places the district in its safest Republican tier.\n\nPrediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-seven chance, and no public general-election polling exists to challenge the fundamentals. The redraw did pull Democratic-leaning parts of Pembroke Pines and Miramar into the district, and Locklin has drawn local media attention and small endorsements, but neither development has attracted outside money or produced evidence of a genuinely competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -10.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0347, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0629, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0423, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0418, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0314, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0905, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0625, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -11.0}]}